                <pb facs="0311" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 St. Pierre-Miquelon/459: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-13T14:00:00+00:00">February 13, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>204. Department’s 80, February 13 [<hi rendition="#italic">12</hi>], 5
                        p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d219-f1"/> The Embassy has now received a formal
                    note from the Foreign Office giving the assurances outlined in the Embassy’s
                    132, January 30, 2 p.m., and indicating that the decree will be issued without
                    modification. The Foreign Office was requested to endeavor to have the
                    promulgation of the decree delayed until the Treasury Department’s further
                    representation had been received. The Foreign Office would only promise to
                    endeavor to have the issuance of the decree delayed until next Wednesday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
